{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"A runaway/exhaustion-truncated completion-verifier run is dispositioned as a BLOCKING\nsubstantive FAIL (exit 1, requires --force) instead of the non-blocking, re-runnable\nINDETERMINATE fault the contract requires (bug 2a6f; 46a2; ed6d). Root cause confirmed (RCA\ncomment). Two compounding seams downstream of a correctly-firing runaway guard, both from\nticket 1d71-a76c-04f6-4642 (commit 6b318ffaec4a).\n\n## Root cause (proven)\n- Seam A (mint): `completion_verdict_assembly._restamp_marker` stamps the per-criterion\n  insufficiency marker only when the criterion's BANK entry carries it; a criterion the abort\n  truncated is NEVER banked (`entry is None`), so the marker is POPPED, minting a bare\n  `met=false` indistinguishable from a positive refutation. The OMITTED-criterion branch of the\n  same function already stamps un-banked criteria insufficient — the ECHO branch is\n  inconsistent.\n- Seam B (disposition): reconcile_verdict already derives the top-level\n  `evidence_sufficient=False` marker on an insufficiency-only FAIL (since 1d71), but the close\n  gate (`close_precheck`) and the standalone `verify-completion` verb (`_llm_commands`) still\n  raise the fail-closed exit 1 for it. Only a `verdict_obtainable=False` fault (the no-criterion\n  fault, bug 2a6f) currently takes the retryable exit-11 path.\n\n## Approach (two behavior-preserving fixes; reuse the EXISTING evidence_sufficient marker)\n- Fix A — `completion_verdict_assembly._restamp_marker`: a finalizer-echoed `met is False`\n  record whose criterion has NO bank entry (`entry is None` — never evaluated/truncated) is\n  stamped `evidence_sufficient=False`, making the echo branch consistent with the omitted\n  branch. Keys STRICTLY on `entry is None`, NOT on any bank-entry evidence-cap `truncated`\n  flag: a PRESENT markerless entry is a genuine refutation and stays bare (failures not masked).\n- Fix B — a single shared pure helper `completion_fail_returncode(result)` (added to\n  completion_reconcile, re-exported from `rebar.llm.completion`) returns the retryable 11 when\n  the FAIL is a fault (`verdict_obtainable is False` OR `evidence_sufficient is False`), else 1.\n  Both consumers call it, so their disposition is identical by construction. NO overload of\n  `verdict_obtainable` (its schema stays the no-criterion fault); routed on the existing\n  `evidence_sufficient` marker. The insufficiency-accurate close message already exists in\n  `_verification_fail_message` — only the returncode changes.\n\n## Impacted sites\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_verdict_assembly.py — `_restamp_marker` (Fix A).\n- src/rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py — new `completion_fail_returncode` helper (Fix B).\n- src/rebar/llm/completion.py — re-export `completion_fail_returncode`.\n- src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py — the generic completion-FAIL raise uses\n  `completion_fail_returncode(result)` for its returncode (was hard-coded 1).\n- src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py — the `verify-completion` verb returns\n  `completion_fail_returncode(result)` on a non-PASS (was hard-coded 1).\n- src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json — update the `evidence_sufficient`\n  description: its close/verb disposition is now the retryable exit-11 fault, not fail-closed.\n- Unchanged consumer (noted for completeness): src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py already\n  persists the top-level `evidence_sufficient` marker onto the durable record (since 1d71) — no\n  new durable-record behavior.\n- tests/ — new deterministic regression tests (no LLM).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] An insufficiency-only FAIL (top-level `evidence_sufficient=False`, incl. un-banked\n  `met=false` echoes) disposes as retryable exit 11 via `completion_fail_returncode`; the\n  ticket does not close.\n- [ ] A completed run with a genuinely-refuted criterion (met=false, no insufficiency marker)\n  still disposes as exit 1 — genuine failures are not masked (dual assertion).\n- [ ] The pre-existing no-criterion fault (`verdict_obtainable=False`, 2a6f) still disposes\n  exit 11 — undisturbed.\n- [ ] `merge_finalizer_with_bank` stamps `evidence_sufficient=False` on an un-banked\n  `met=false` echo (entry is None), and leaves a present markerless entry bare.\n- [ ] `verdict_obtainable`'s schema/meaning is unchanged (no overload); `evidence_sufficient`\n  schema doc updated to the retryable disposition.\n- [ ] Deterministic regression tests (no LLM) cover all; `make lint` + `make typecheck` clean;\n  complexity ratchet not increased.\n\n## Portability\nNo CI-provider coupling: pure in-process verdict reconciliation/assembly/disposition logic,\nexercised by deterministic unit tests that run under any/no CI provider.\n\n## Test plan\nHeld-out RED oracle drives `merge_finalizer_with_bank` and the shared\n`completion_fail_returncode` helper on synthetic verdict/bank dicts; asserts the exit-11\ninsufficiency disposition, the preserved 2a6f exit-11 fault, and the non-masking exit-1 genuine\nblock; mutation-check by restoring the pop / collapsing the helper to always-1."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787672469998961001,"uuid":"028ab68b-bfa5-4879-9b7c-0d5f7f6bf303"}